  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.read_source.fn` has one obligation. Criterion code must use `ValidationContext.read_source` for this operation. That obligation is a signature and usage convention. The behavior behind it belongs to the cited `ValidationContext.read_source` requirement and to the sibling `read_source.behavior` and `read_source.inputs` requirements, and I did not reassess those.\n\nThe only supplied test, `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[direct_source_reads_preserve_mapping_errors_and_record_only_successful_returns]`, is marked `{test}` for this requirement. It calls `ValidationContext::read_source(&OutlineData)` and gets `Result<D::NodeContent, D::Error>`. This matches the contract the cited requirement declares, `read_source(&self, item: &OutlineData)`. The test also checks the following:\n- Unsupported items return an error that contains `unsupported source item`.\n- A failed read returns an error that contains `prepared source read failed`.\n- A successful read returns the content, here `prepared contents`.\n- A successful read records a `Dependency::Node(node, fingerprint)`, and failed reads record nothing.\n- The record is current until the contents change, after which `is_current` returns false.\n\nThe impl sites are `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs` (`fn[read_source]`) and `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources.rs` (`SourceAnalysis::parse`). `parse` is the criterion-side code that uses `read_source`. The requirement states no further testable obligation, such as a failure case or a distinct mode, so I found no unexercised obligation or boundary.",
